workbench-trust-prompt-title = Trust the project { $project }?
workbench-trust-prompt-body = Its build can run code on this computer: until you trust it, the IDE runs none of its build scripts by itself, does not import it with Gradle, starts the Java language server without Lombok and annotation processors, and leaves out the Go environment of .zen/go.json. Trust it only if you trust where it comes from.
workbench-trust-action = Trust Project
workbench-trust-agent = Only the person trusts a project; agents cannot.
workbench-trust-agent-build = The project { $project } is not trusted: agents may not run its build. The person can trust it with Trust Project.
workbench-trust-no-project = No project is open.
workbench-trust-no-data = The IDE has no data folder to keep the trusted projects in.
workbench-trust-write = The trusted projects could not be saved: { $error }
workbench-trust-not-folder = { $path } is not a folder.
workbench-trust-run = { $name } does not start: the project is opened in safe mode, where nothing runs or debugs. Trust the project (Trust Project) first.
workbench-trust-before-launch = { $name } runs programs before launch, and the project is not trusted: trust the project (Trust Project) first.
workbench-trust-agent-build-setting = An agent may not change { $key }: it chooses the program or the JVM arguments the build runs with. The person can change it in the settings.
workbench-trust-build-load = { $project } is not trusted, so its build was not loaded: loading it runs the build's own code. Trust the project to load it.
workbench-trust-artifacts = The artifacts of { $project } build with its build and are written where the project says, and the project is not trusted: trust the project (Trust Project) first.
workbench-trust-file-watchers = The file watchers of { $project } came with the project, and the project is not trusted: trust it (Trust Project) to run them.
